# Documentation

Writing for agents: load `writing-for-agents` when editing skills, `AGENTS.md`, or other always-loaded pointers. Domain terms and decisions: `domain-modeling`.

## Glossary

- Live terms go in `GLOSSARY.md` at the repo root (single-context). Create it lazily when a term is actually resolved.
- Use glossary words in issues, tests, and code names. Do not drift to avoided synonyms.
- Missing glossary: proceed silently. Do not nag to create it up front.

## ADRs

- Path: `docs/adr/NNNN-slug.md`. Create the directory on the first ADR.
- Scan existing numbers and increment. One paragraph is enough: context, decision, why.
- Write an ADR only when all three hold: **hard to reverse**, **surprising without context**, **a real trade-off**.
- If new work contradicts an ADR, say so explicitly. Do not silently override.

## AGENTS.md vs rules vs skills

- `AGENTS.md`: always-on, tiny, pointers only.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`: Cursor topic guidance.
- `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`: procedures. Do not copy a skill into a rule; point at it.
